# Copy this file to `.env.local` (which is gitignored).
#
#   cp .env.local.example .env.local
#   # then edit .env.local
#
# There is no AI key to set. Inference runs on Workers AI through the `AI`
# binding declared in wrangler.jsonc, so the Worker is authorised by being the
# Worker. Nothing here is a credential; everything below is optional.

# Optional — any text-generation model id from the Workers AI catalogue.
# AI_MODEL=@cf/meta/llama-4-scout-17b-16e-instruct

# Optional — gate the deployment behind a shared code. When set, the AI routes
# reject any request that does not send it, so a leaked link cannot spend your
# daily inference allowance. Treat this one as a real secret.
# APP_ACCESS_CODE=

# Optional — durable, cross-instance rate limiting for /api/*. Without these the
# limiter is in-memory and resets whenever the Worker is recycled.
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# Local development note: Workers AI has no local emulator. `next dev` proxies
# the binding to the real service, which needs a logged-in wrangler:
#
#   npx wrangler login
#
# Without it the three AI pages still render and return a clear
# "Workers AI is not bound" message instead of a draft.
